# Question 1
### Case Manipulation and Counting

Given the DNA sequence `"agctTAGCta"`, use string methods to:
* Convert it to all uppercase
* Convert it to all lowercase
* Count how many times 'a' appears (case-insensitive)
<br>

# Question 2
### Character Type Checking

Use appropriate string methods to:
* Check if `"ATCG123"` contains only letters
* Check if `"12345"` contains only numbers
* Check if `"ATCG"` contains only letters
<br></br>

# Question 3
### Splitting and Joining

Given the string `"ATCG-TAGC-GCTA"`, use string methods to:
* Split the sequence at each dash
* Join the resulting sequences with '|' instead of dashes
<br></br>

# Question 4
### Pattern Checking

Using the string methods covered, write code to:
* Check if `"ATATATCG"` starts with `"ATA"`
* Check if `"GCGCTAT"` ends with `"TAT"`
* Find the position of `"GC"` in `"ATGCTA"`
<br></br>

# Question 5
### Advanced Counting

Use the string method `count()` with different start and end parameters on `"ATAGATAGATAG"` to:
* Count total occurrences of `"TAG"`
* Count occurrences of `"TAG"` in first 6 characters only
* Count occurrences of `"TAG"` between positions 3 and 9
<br></br>
